            "review_title": "Review at Ryuko",
            "review_text": "Biologywelch\nLeuchars, United Kingdom91 contributions\n0\nAssorted internal organs! Best part of cheek!\nJun 2017 • Couples\nThis was our first time visiting this type of Japanese BBQ restaurant and it was utterly delicious. \n\nWe ordered a selection of unusual cuts of meat - diaphragm, best part of tongue, cheek... Assorted internal organs! First stomach! The list goes on! You may be thinking, 'that's a gimmick for westerners' (if you're a Westerner), but you'd be WRONG! Each piece of meat was cut ultra thin, with immaculate precision, and presented beautifully with some garnish. The marinade on the meat was delicious and as the meat cooked on the BBQ you could see it crisp up and dripping it's delicious juices into the fire, the smell was delicious...\n\nIt's making me hungry just thinking about it! The sweet marinade of the melt in your mouth cuts of meat, cooked over BBQ was exquisite. I would thoroughly recommend this restaurant, particularly to other Brits if you are up for something a bit different and nevertheless mouth-wateringly tasty. Please set one up in Colchester, Essex!\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 17, 2017",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
